    "tips": {
      "csv": "粘贴以逗号分隔、带表头且至少有一行数据的 CSV。停止输入 0.3 秒后，JSON 会自动更新。支持引号字段中的逗号、换行和双写引号。",
      "json": "粘贴非空的 JSON 对象数组。停止输入 0.3 秒后，CSV 会自动更新。嵌套对象展开为点路径列；数组和空对象写成 JSON 文本。",
      "parseTypes": "CSV → JSON 时转换未加引号的数字、true、false 和 null。带引号的值、前导零值和超出安全范围的整数保持为文本。更改此选项会重新转换当前 CSV。",
      "emptyNull": "CSV → JSON 时，将未加引号的空字段写成 null，而非空字符串。带引号的空字段仍是字符串。更改此选项会重新转换当前 CSV。",
      "clear": "清空两个面板、状态和等待执行的转换，保留选项。焦点在工具内时，Ctrl+L（Mac 为 ⌘+L）也会清空。",
      "copyCsv": "复制 CSV 面板内当前的全部文本，包括您编辑的内容。面板为空时无法复制。",
      "copyJson": "复制 JSON 面板内当前的全部文本，包括您编辑的内容。面板为空时无法复制。"
    }
  },
  "ja": {
    "copy": "コピー",
    "copied": "コピー済み！",
    "copyFailed": "コピー失敗",
    "clear": "クリア",
    "convertedToJson": "{n} 行を JSON に変換しました。",
    "convertedToCsv": "{n} 行を CSV に変換しました。",
    "errorPrefix": "エラー：",
    "parseTypes": "数値・真偽値を自動変換",
    "emptyNull": "空フィールド → null",
    "renamedHeaders": "重複したヘッダー名を変更しました：{list}。",
    "addedKeys": "ヘッダーより項目が多い行があるため、次のキーを追加しました：{cols}。",
    "errNeedRows": "CSV にはヘッダー行とデータ行が 1 行以上必要です。",
    "errNotArray": "JSON はオブジェクトの配列である必要があります。",
    "errEmptyArray": "JSON 配列が空です。",
    "errItem": "{n} 番目の要素はオブジェクトである必要があります。",
    "errUnclosed": "{line} 行目で始まる引用符付きフィールドが閉じられていません。閉じる \" を追加するか、開始の \" を削除してください。",
    "numbersAsText": "このブラウザーでは次の数値を正確に保持できないため、文字列として書き出しました：{list}。",
    "tips": {
      "csv": "ヘッダーと1行以上のデータを含むカンマ区切りの CSV を貼り付けます。入力を止めて0.3秒後に JSON が更新されます。引用符内のカンマ、改行、二重に書いた引用符に対応します。",
      "json": "空でない JSON オブジェクト配列を貼り付けます。入力を止めて0.3秒後に CSV が更新されます。ネストしたオブジェクトはドット区切りの列に展開し、配列と空のオブジェクトは JSON テキストとして書きます。",
      "parseTypes": "CSV → JSON で、引用符のない数値、true、false、null を変換します。引用符付きの値、先頭が0の値、安全な範囲を超える整数は文字列のままです。変更すると現在の CSV を再変換します。",
      "emptyNull": "CSV → JSON で、引用符のない空フィールドを空文字列ではなく null にします。引用符付きの空フィールドは文字列のままです。変更すると現在の CSV を再変換します。",
      "clear": "両方の欄、ステータス、待機中の変換をクリアし、オプションは保持します。ツール内にフォーカスがある場合は Ctrl+L（Mac は ⌘+L）でもクリアできます。",
      "copyCsv": "編集内容を含む CSV 欄の現在の全文をコピーします。空の欄はコピーできません。",
      "copyJson": "編集内容を含む JSON 欄の現在の全文をコピーします。空の欄はコピーできません。"
    }
  },
  "ko": {
    "copy": "복사",
    "copied": "복사됨!",
    "copyFailed": "복사 실패",
    "clear": "지우기",
    "convertedToJson": "{n}행을 JSON으로 변환했습니다.",
    "convertedToCsv": "{n}행을 CSV로 변환했습니다.",
    "errorPrefix": "오류: ",
    "parseTypes": "숫자 및 불리언 추론",
    "emptyNull": "빈 필드 → null",
    "renamedHeaders": "중복된 헤더 이름을 바꿨습니다: {list}.",
    "addedKeys": "헤더보다 필드가 많은 행이 있어 다음 키를 추가했습니다: {cols}.",
    "errNeedRows": "CSV에는 헤더 행과 데이터 행이 하나 이상 있어야 합니다.",
    "errNotArray": "JSON은 객체 배열이어야 합니다.",
    "errEmptyArray": "JSON 배열이 비어 있습니다.",
    "errItem": "{n}번째 항목은 객체여야 합니다.",
    "errUnclosed": "{line}행에서 시작한 따옴표 필드가 닫히지 않았습니다. 닫는 \"를 추가하거나 여는 \"를 지우세요.",
    "numbersAsText": "이 브라우저는 다음 숫자를 정확히 유지할 수 없어 텍스트로 썼습니다: {list}.",
    "tips": {
      "csv": "헤더와 데이터 행이 하나 이상 있는 쉼표 구분 CSV를 붙여 넣습니다. 입력을 멈추고 0.3초 후 JSON이 갱신됩니다. 따옴표 안의 쉼표, 줄바꿈, 두 번 쓴 따옴표를 지원합니다.",
      "json": "비어 있지 않은 JSON 객체 배열을 붙여 넣습니다. 입력을 멈추고 0.3초 후 CSV가 갱신됩니다. 중첩 객체는 점 경로 열로 펼치고 배열과 빈 객체는 JSON 텍스트로 씁니다.",
      "parseTypes": "CSV → JSON에서 따옴표 없는 숫자, true, false, null을 변환합니다. 따옴표가 있는 값, 앞자리 0이 있는 값, 안전한 범위를 넘는 정수는 문자열로 남습니다. 옵션을 바꾸면 현재 CSV를 다시 변환합니다.",
      "emptyNull": "CSV → JSON에서 따옴표 없는 빈 필드를 빈 문자열 대신 null로 씁니다. 따옴표로 감싼 빈 필드는 문자열로 남습니다. 옵션을 바꾸면 현재 CSV를 다시 변환합니다.",
      "clear": "두 패널, 상태와 대기 중인 변환을 지우고 옵션은 유지합니다. 도구 안에 포커스가 있으면 Ctrl+L(Mac은 ⌘+L)로도 지울 수 있습니다.",
      "copyCsv": "편집 내용을 포함한 CSV 패널의 현재 전체 텍스트를 복사합니다. 빈 패널은 복사할 수 없습니다.",
      "copyJson": "편집 내용을 포함한 JSON 패널의 현재 전체 텍스트를 복사합니다. 빈 패널은 복사할 수 없습니다."
    }
  }
};
// strings:end
const T = STRINGS[lang] || STRINGS.en;
const { tips: TIPS, ...CLIENT } = T;
---

<div class="cj-wrap" data-strings={JSON.stringify(CLIENT)}>
  <div class="cj-toolbar">
    <div class="cj-control">
      <label class="cj-checkbox-label"><input type="checkbox" id="cj-parse-types" checked /><span>{T.parseTypes}</span></label>
      <Toggletip id="cj-tip-parse-types" about={T.parseTypes} lang={lang}>{TIPS.parseTypes}</Toggletip>
    </div>
    <div class="cj-control">
      <label class="cj-checkbox-label"><input type="checkbox" id="cj-empty-null" /><span>{T.emptyNull}</span></label>
      <Toggletip id="cj-tip-empty-null" about={T.emptyNull} lang={lang}>{TIPS.emptyNull}</Toggletip>
    </div>
    <div class="cj-control">
      <button id="cj-clear" class="btn-ghost" type="button">{T.clear}</button>
      <Toggletip id="cj-tip-clear" about={T.clear} lang={lang}>{TIPS.clear}</Toggletip>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div id="cj-status" class="cj-status" aria-live="polite"></div>
  <div class="cj-panels zt-io">
    <div class="cj-panel zt-io-pane">
      <div class="cj-head">
        <div class="cj-control"><label for="cj-csv">CSV</label><Toggletip id="cj-tip-csv" about="CSV" lang={lang}>{TIPS.csv}</Toggletip></div>
        <div class="cj-control"><button id="cj-copy-csv" class="btn-copy" type="button">{T.copy}</button><Toggletip id="cj-tip-copy-csv" about={T.copy + ' CSV'} lang={lang}>{TIPS.copyCsv}</Toggletip></div>
      </div>
      <textarea id="cj-csv" class="tool-textarea cj-box zt-io-fill" placeholder="name,age,city&#10;Alice,30,&quot;New York&quot;&#10;Bob,25,London" spellcheck="false"></textarea>
    </div>
    <div class="cj-panel zt-io-pane">
      <div class="cj-head">
        <div class="cj-control"><label for="cj-json">JSON</label><Toggletip id="cj-tip-json" about="JSON" lang={lang}>{TIPS.json}</Toggletip></div>
        <div class="cj-control"><button id="cj-copy-json" class="btn-copy" type="button">{T.copy}</button><Toggletip id="cj-tip-copy-json" about={T.copy + ' JSON'} lang={lang}>{TIPS.copyJson}</Toggletip></div>
      </div>
      <textarea id="cj-json" class="tool-textarea cj-box zt-io-fill" placeholder='[{"name":"Alice","age":"30","city":"New York"}]' spellcheck="false"></textarea>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var t = JSON.parse(document.querySelector('.cj-wrap').dataset.strings || '{}');

      function rowMsg(tmpl, n) {
        return tmpl.replace('{n}', n).replace('{s}', n === 1 ? '' : 's');
      }

      var csvEl = document.getElementById('cj-csv');
      var jsonEl = document.getElementById('cj-json');
      var statusEl = document.getElementById('cj-status');
      var copyCsvBtn = document.getElementById('cj-copy-csv');
      var copyJsonBtn = document.getElementById('cj-copy-json');
      var parseTypesEl = document.getElementById('cj-parse-types');
      var emptyNullEl = document.getElementById('cj-empty-null');
      var lastValidJsonOutput = '';
      var lastValidCsvOutput = '';
      var copyStates = [
        { button: copyCsvBtn, revision: 0, timer: null },
        { button: copyJsonBtn, revision: 0, timer: null }
      ];

      function setStatus(msg, isError) {
        statusEl.textContent = msg;
        statusEl.className = 'cj-status ' + (isError ? 'error' : 'success');
      }

      function clearStatus() {
        statusEl.textContent = '';
        statusEl.className = 'cj-status';
      }

      /* ── engine:start ── */
      function escapeCsvField(val) {
        if (/[",\n\r]/.test(val)) {
          return '"' + val.replace(/"/g, '""') + '"';
        }
        return val;
      }

      function isPlainObject(v) {
        return v !== null && typeof v === 'object' && !Array.isArray(v) && !(JSON.isRawJSON && JSON.isRawJSON(v));
      }

      /* Nested objects become dot-path columns (user.name); arrays and empty objects stay whole as JSON text. */
      function flattenRow(obj, prefix, out) {
        var keys = Object.keys(obj);
        for (var k = 0; k < keys.length; k++) {
          var path = prefix + keys[k];
          var v = obj[keys[k]];
          if (isPlainObject(v) && Object.keys(v).length > 0) flattenRow(v, path + '.', out);
          else out.set(path, v);
        }
        return out;
      }

      function csvCell(v) {
        if (v === null || v === undefined) return '';
        if (typeof v === 'object') return JSON.stringify(v);
        return String(v);
      }

      function jsonToCsv(data) {
        if (!Array.isArray(data)) throw new Error('JSON must be an array of objects.');
        if (data.length === 0) throw new Error('JSON array is empty.');
        var rows = [];
        var headers = [];
        var seen = new Set();
        for (var i = 0; i < data.length; i++) {
          if (!isPlainObject(data[i])) throw new Error('Item ' + (i + 1) + ' must be a plain object.');
          var flat = flattenRow(data[i], '', new Map());
          flat.forEach(function (_, path) {
            if (!seen.has(path)) { seen.add(path); headers.push(path); }
          });
          rows.push(flat);
        }
        var lines = [headers.map(escapeCsvField).join(',')];
        for (var r = 0; r < rows.length; r++) {
          var cells = [];
          for (var h = 0; h < headers.length; h++) cells.push(escapeCsvField(csvCell(rows[r].get(headers[h]))));
          lines.push(cells.join(','));
        }
        return lines.join('\n');
      }

      /* A number text is exact when the JavaScript number keeps its value: finite, not -0 (JSON
         writes it as 0), not rounded to 0, and with the same significant digits. */
      function sigDigits(text) {
        return text.replace(/^-/, '').split(/[eE]/)[0].replace('.', '').replace(/^0+/, '').replace(/0+$/, '');
      }
      function isExactNumber(text, n) {
        if (!isFinite(n) || Object.is(n, -0)) return false;
        if (n === 0) return !/[1-9]/.test(text.split(/[eE]/)[0]);
        return sigDigits(text) === sigDigits(String(n));
      }

      /* ── Type inference for a single CSV field value ── */
      function inferValue(raw, quoted, parseTypes, emptyNull) {
        if (quoted) return raw;
        if (raw === '') return emptyNull ? null : raw;
        if (!parseTypes) return raw;
        var lo = raw.toLowerCase();
        if (lo === 'null') return null;
        if (lo === 'true') return true;
        if (lo === 'false') return false;
        /* number: only the RFC 8259 §6 number syntax (no +, leading zeros, bare . or spaces) */
        if (!/^-?(?:0|[1-9]\d*)(?:\.\d+)?(?:[eE][+-]?\d+)?$/.test(raw)) return raw;
        var n = Number(raw);
        /* reject integers that exceed safe range to avoid precision loss */
        if (Number.isInteger(n) && !Number.isSafeInteger(n)) return raw;
        return isExactNumber(raw, n) ? n : raw;
      }

      /* ── CSV parser: handles quoted fields; tracks per-field quoted status ── */
      function parseCsv(text) {
        var rows = [];
        var quotedFlags = []; /* parallel array: quotedFlags[r][c] === true when field was quoted */
        var row = [];
        var rowQ = [];
        var field = '';
        var wasQuoted = false;
        var inQuote = false;
        var quoteStart = 0;
        var i = 0;
        var len = text.length;

        while (i < len) {
          var ch = text[i];
          if (inQuote) {
            if (ch === '"') {
              if (i + 1 < len && text[i + 1] === '"') {
                field += '"';
                i += 2;
              } else {
                inQuote = false;
                i++;
              }
            } else {
              field += ch;
              i++;
            }
          } else {
            if (ch === '"' && field === '' && !wasQuoted) {
              /* a quote opens a quoted field only at the start of the field; elsewhere it is text */
              inQuote = true;
              wasQuoted = true;
              quoteStart = i;
              i++;
            } else if (ch === ',') {
              row.push(field);
              rowQ.push(wasQuoted);
              field = '';
              wasQuoted = false;
              i++;
            } else if (ch === '\r') {
              row.push(field);
              rowQ.push(wasQuoted);
              field = '';
              wasQuoted = false;
              rows.push(row);
              quotedFlags.push(rowQ);
              row = [];
              rowQ = [];
              i++;
              if (i < len && text[i] === '\n') i++;
            } else if (ch === '\n') {
              row.push(field);
              rowQ.push(wasQuoted);
              field = '';
              wasQuoted = false;
              rows.push(row);
              quotedFlags.push(rowQ);
              row = [];
              rowQ = [];
              i++;
            } else {
              field += ch;
              i++;
            }
          }
        }

        if (inQuote) throw new Error('Unclosed quote starting on line ' + text.slice(0, quoteStart).split(/\r\n|\r|\n/).length + '.');

        /* last field / row */
        if (field || row.length > 0) {
          row.push(field);
          rowQ.push(wasQuoted);
          rows.push(row);
          quotedFlags.push(rowQ);
        }

        /* drop trailing empty row */
        if (rows.length > 0) {
          var last = rows[rows.length - 1];
          if (last.length === 1 && last[0] === '') {
            rows.pop();
            quotedFlags.pop();
          }
        }

        return { rows: rows, quotedFlags: quotedFlags };
      }
      /* ── engine:end ── */

      /* Keys are never lost: a repeated header name gets _2, _3 …; fields beyond the header
         get column_N (N = position). Objects have no prototype, so __proto__ is a normal key. */
      function buildJsonFromCsv(raw) {
        var parsed = parseCsv(raw);
        var rows = parsed.rows;
        var quotedFlags = parsed.quotedFlags;
        if (rows.length < 2) throw new Error(t.errNeedRows);
        var colCount = rows[0].length;
        for (var w = 1; w < rows.length; w++) if (rows[w].length > colCount) colCount = rows[w].length;
        var written = new Set(rows[0]);
        var taken = new Set();
        var headers = [];
        var renamed = [];
        var added = [];
        for (var h = 0; h < colCount; h++) {
          var base = h < rows[0].length ? rows[0][h] : 'column_' + (h + 1);
          var name = base;
          if (taken.has(name) || (h >= rows[0].length && written.has(name))) {
            for (var k = 2; taken.has(base + '_' + k) || written.has(base + '_' + k); k++) {}
            name = base + '_' + k;
          }
          if (h >= rows[0].length) added.push(name);
          else if (name !== base) renamed.push(base + ' → ' + name);
          taken.add(name);
          headers.push(name);
        }
        var parseTypes = parseTypesEl.checked;
        var emptyNull = emptyNullEl.checked;
        var result = [];
        for (var r = 1; r < rows.length; r++) {
          var obj = Object.create(null);
          for (var c = 0; c < headers.length; c++) {
            var rawVal = rows[r][c] !== undefined ? rows[r][c] : '';
            var isQuoted = quotedFlags[r] ? !!quotedFlags[r][c] : false;
            obj[headers[c]] = inferValue(rawVal, isQuoted, parseTypes, emptyNull);
          }
          result.push(obj);
        }
        return { rows: result, renamed: renamed, added: added };
      }

      /* Drop a BOM, leading blank lines and trailing line breaks only, so spaces at the end of the last field stay. */
      function leadingLines(text) {
        var lead = /^(?:[ \t]*(?:\r\n|\r|\n))+/.exec(text.replace(/^\uFEFF/, ''));
        return lead ? lead[0].split(/\r\n|\r|\n/).length - 1 : 0;
      }
      function csvSource(text) {
        return text.replace(/^\uFEFF/, '').replace(/^(?:[ \t]*(?:\r\n|\r|\n))+/, '').replace(/(?:\r\n|\r|\n)[ \t\r\n]*$/, '');
      }

      /* The engine reports input errors in English; show them in the page language. lineOffset is the
         number of lines removed before the text reached the engine, so the line matches the textarea. */
      function localError(message, lineOffset) {
        var unclosed = /^Unclosed quote starting on line (\d+)\.$/.exec(message);
        if (unclosed) return t.errUnclosed.replace('{line}', String(Number(unclosed[1]) + (lineOffset || 0)));
        if (message === 'JSON must be an array of objects.') return t.errNotArray;
        if (message === 'JSON array is empty.') return t.errEmptyArray;
        var item = /^Item (\d+) must be a plain object\.$/.exec(message);
        return item ? t.errItem.replace('{n}', item[1]) : message;
      }

      /* JSON → CSV: the browser's JSON.parse rounds numbers that a double cannot hold
         (12345678901234567890, 1e-400, -0). Where JSON.rawJSON and the reviver's source text
         exist (Chrome 114, Firefox 135, Safari 18.4), such numbers keep their source text.
         Elsewhere they are quoted before parsing, so they reach the CSV as text, never rounded. */
      var sourceProbe = false;
      try { JSON.parse('1', function (k, v, ctx) { if (ctx && ctx.source === '1') sourceProbe = true; return v; }); } catch (e) {}
      var keepsSource = sourceProbe && typeof JSON.rawJSON === 'function';

      function lossyNumbers(text) {
        var found = [];
        var num = /-?(?:0|[1-9]\d*)(?:\.\d+)?(?:[eE][+-]?\d+)?/y;
        for (var i = 0; i < text.length;) {
          var ch = text[i];
          if (ch === '"') {
            for (i++; i < text.length && text[i] !== '"'; i += text[i] === '\\' ? 2 : 1) {}
            i++;
          } else if (ch === '-' || (ch >= '0' && ch <= '9')) {
            num.lastIndex = i;
            var m = num.exec(text);
            if (!m) { i++; continue; }
            if (!isExactNumber(m[0], Number(m[0]))) found.push({ start: i, text: m[0] });
            i += m[0].length;
          } else i++;
        }
        return found;
      }

      function parseJsonInput(raw) {
        var data = JSON.parse(raw);
        var lossy = lossyNumbers(raw);
        if (!lossy.length) return { data: data, asText: [] };
        if (keepsSource) {
          data = JSON.parse(raw, function (k, v, ctx) {
            return typeof v === 'number' && ctx && typeof ctx.source === 'string' && !isExactNumber(ctx.source, v) ? JSON.rawJSON(ctx.source) : v;
          });
          return { data: data, asText: [] };
        }
        var quoted = '';
        var last = 0;
        lossy.forEach(function (tok) {
          quoted += raw.slice(last, tok.start) + '"' + tok.text + '"';
          last = tok.start + tok.text.length;
        });
        return { data: JSON.parse(quoted + raw.slice(last)), asText: lossy.map(function (tok) { return tok.text; }) };
      }

      /* ── Real-time CSV → JSON (debounced 300ms) ── */
      var _csvLiveTimer = null;
      csvEl.addEventListener('input', function () {
        cancelConversions();
        resetCopies();
        _csvLiveTimer = setTimeout(function () {
          resetCopies();
          if (!csvEl.value.trim()) { jsonEl.value = ''; lastValidJsonOutput = ''; clearStatus(); return; }
          try {
            var built = buildJsonFromCsv(csvSource(csvEl.value));
            jsonEl.value = JSON.stringify(built.rows, null, 2);
            lastValidJsonOutput = jsonEl.value;
            var msg = rowMsg(t.convertedToJson, built.rows.length);
            if (built.renamed.length) msg += ' ' + t.renamedHeaders.replace('{list}', built.renamed.join(', '));
            if (built.added.length) msg += ' ' + t.addedKeys.replace('{cols}', built.added.join(', '));
            setStatus(msg, false);
          } catch (e) {
            jsonEl.value = '';
            lastValidJsonOutput = '';
            setStatus(t.errorPrefix + localError(e.message, leadingLines(csvEl.value)), true);
          }
        }, 300);
      });

      /* re-run live conversion when options change */
      parseTypesEl.addEventListener('change', function () {
        if (csvEl.value.trim()) csvEl.dispatchEvent(new Event('input'));
      });
      emptyNullEl.addEventListener('change', function () {
        if (csvEl.value.trim()) csvEl.dispatchEvent(new Event('input'));
      });

      /* ── Real-time JSON → CSV (debounced 300ms) ── */
      var _jsonLiveTimer = null;
      jsonEl.addEventListener('input', function () {
        cancelConversions();
        resetCopies();
        _jsonLiveTimer = setTimeout(function () {
          resetCopies();
          var raw = jsonEl.value.trim();
          if (!raw) { csvEl.value = ''; lastValidCsvOutput = ''; clearStatus(); return; }
          try {
            var parsedJson = parseJsonInput(raw);
            var data = parsedJson.data;
            csvEl.value = jsonToCsv(data);
            lastValidCsvOutput = csvEl.value;
            var csvMsg = rowMsg(t.convertedToCsv, data.length);
            if (parsedJson.asText.length) csvMsg += ' ' + t.numbersAsText.replace('{list}', parsedJson.asText.join(', '));
            setStatus(csvMsg, false);
          } catch (e) {
            csvEl.value = '';
            lastValidCsvOutput = '';
            setStatus(t.errorPrefix + localError(e.message), true);
          }
        }, 300);
      });

      /* ── Clear ── */
      function cancelConversions() {
        clearTimeout(_csvLiveTimer);
        clearTimeout(_jsonLiveTimer);
      }

      function clearAll() {
        cancelConversions();
        resetCopies();
        csvEl.focus();
        csvEl.value = '';
        jsonEl.value = '';
        lastValidJsonOutput = '';
        lastValidCsvOutput = '';
        clearStatus();
      }
      document.getElementById('cj-clear').addEventListener('click', clearAll);
      document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
        if (!(e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey) || e.key.toLowerCase() !== 'l') return;
        var widget = document.querySelector('.cj-wrap');
        if (!widget || !widget.contains(document.activeElement)) return;
        e.preventDefault();
        clearAll();
      });

      /* ── Copy buttons ── */
      function resetCopies() {
        copyStates.forEach(function (state) {
          state.revision++;
          clearTimeout(state.timer);
          state.button.textContent = t.copy;
        });
      }

      function copyText(state, text) {
        if (!text) return;
        var revision = ++state.revision;
        clearTimeout(state.timer);
        function failed() {
          if (revision === state.revision) state.button.textContent = t.copyFailed;
        }
        try {
          navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(function () {
            if (revision !== state.revision) return;
            state.button.textContent = t.copied;
            state.timer = setTimeout(function () {
              if (revision === state.revision) state.button.textContent = t.copy;
            }, 1500);
          }, failed);
        } catch (e) { failed(); }
      }

      copyCsvBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
        copyText(copyStates[0], csvEl.value);
      });

      copyJsonBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
        copyText(copyStates[1], jsonEl.value);
      });
    })();
  </script>
</div>

